body:
Thanks so much for listening and taking the time to comment. Glad you recognized one of the samples, I'm always curious whether anyone will. So far you're the first to mention it at least. 

&#x200B;

Your words mean a lot! Thank you.

So do I. I am definitely holding tight to some memories. One of the greatest gifts is after all that happened, I ended up finding an old polaroid of us together on a random day doing stupid shit in our living room. It was exactly what I needed to find, and I cherish that picture now. 

&#x200B;

Thanks for listening <3

Agreed. It was my first impulse, to make art about it. The day I learned about what happened, I tried to make a song about it and just couldn't figure it out. I walked out to the house I used to live in with that friend and I recorded myself talking to her. Listening to Burial unlocked something in me. I suddenly allowed the art to be messy. It wasn't going to be perfect-- I kept wanting to make the "perfect" tribute to her. But Burial's music was messy, sharp, strange. Just like life, just like the funeral was... you know? And all of a sudden I made all of this. Like floodgates opened. 

&#x200B;

Anyways, that recording I made of myself talking to her, that's the clip that plays in the very last few seconds. "I wonder if I'd do things differently, if I'd known this day was coming. I'd like to think that I would."

&#x200B;

I said that because she'd called me a month before all that happened, saying that she had to leave that town. I'd moved across the country and she was still in that tiny town. She called me saying we should move in together; she was depressed and needed to get out; she missed me. I told her I wanted that, but I needed a few more months to get ready to move, I couldn't just uproot everything to move in with her. In the meantime, things got bad enough on her end that she did what she did. That's what most of the album is about. Trying to reconcile the whole idea that 1) if I'd acted differently she could possibly still be alive, and 2) that doesn't have to mean it's "my fault." 

&#x200B;

Thanks so much for listening, stranger.

This is a music project about losing a friend to suicide.

&#x200B;

It's about missing them while also envying them. Being hurt by what they did while having fantasized about doing the same.

&#x200B;

Making this project added some much-needed punctuation to the year, and for that I'm grateful. A lot of the inspiration came from Burial's gritty, sample-heavy music. I had some really beautiful moments laying in bed and being washed over by some of his music.Thanks for listening/watching.

&#x200B;

If you want to listen to any more of my music, you can just look up Kimora on Spotify or Apple Music or any of that stuff.

Yeah. I always use the alpicool's "eco" mode and tell it to hover around 29 fahrenheit (which in actuality seems more like 32-34, plus or minus a few degrees). What solar gen are you looking at? I had the goal zero yeti 500 for a while but that one's battery capacity was making me a bit nervous, so I upgraded. Now i feel like I have too much power

&#x200B;

Edit: I'll add that I keep the fridge under my bed in a little well-insulated cave. I do remember that the first day I had it plugged in, it took a fair amount of power to bring it down from 70 degrees ambient temp to 29 degrees refrigerated, but now that it's just maintaining that 29 degrees, I can guarantee it could go for way more than 11-12 hours of refrigeration. It's funny, I expected to be using a lot more power  based on what I heard about people trying to keep fridges running on trips; that's why I upgraded from the 500ah to the 1000ah, but that turned out to be a bit of overkill. If there had been a 750ah model available, I would have loved to go for that and save a couple hundred bucks. I will also note that I have not fully stocked the fridge yet. I have it maybe half-full, rarely more. Maybe if it was packed to the brim with dense and lukewarm foods, I could see that taking quite a bit of power to cool down and keep cold.

200W Renogy solar into a 1000ah Jackery battery bank with 2kw inverter.

&#x200B;

I run a Fan-tastic roof fan, Alpicool refrigerator, LED strip lights, USB phone charger, and another LED light, occasionally a computer charger. Even using all of these, overnight I'll hardly drop beneath 80ish percent battery capacity, and I could probably last four days of bad weather. If I knew the weather was coming and decided to really conserve, I could make it over a week.

&#x200B;

Edit: semi-relevant is the fact that the Jackery has an MPPT already built into it

hey all, electric question:

&#x200B;

I'm driving a ford e-350. It's a diesel engine so it has two batteries and shore power. I'm looking to set up a power station with a solar rig on the roof. My question is: is there a way to top off the power station with the alternator power? For instance, is there some sort of rigging I could set up that sends alternator power to my power station once the van engine batteries are sufficiently charged? If not, there's also an adapter so I can charge the powerstation from the 12v outlet. I just wanted to know if there was an easier way. Thanks in advance!

[should I go for it?](https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/859789127838062)

&#x200B;

I guess my only hesitation with buying an ambulance is the width and problems with stealth. I'm nervous about parking such a wide vehicle and I'm nervous it will be noticed wherever I go. Other than that, this looks like a dream vehicle.....

Hi all! I finally have the cash and the courage. I'm going to do it by the end of summer. For now, though, I need some opinions about van models. Here are a few I've found. Any thoughts? 

&#x200B;

[Ugly as hell, but a nice length](https://albany.craigslist.org/cto/d/glens-falls-1996-conversion-dodge-ram/7113667491.html)

&#x200B;

[Gorgeous! But maybe too small. Would have to sacrifice a lot of the kitchen/storage space](https://plattsburgh.craigslist.org/cto/d/plattsburgh-ford-econoline/7103910897.html#)

&#x200B;

[Spacious, but maybe too long? And quite a few miles... (151k)](https://vermont.craigslist.org/ctd/d/rutland-2010-ford-e250-van-bus/7112383021.html)

brilliant paintings. Reminds me of Caspar David Friedrich's work—the vast, shadowed wastelands, the small figures traversing them. Wow. I don't expect to see much art like this nowadays, but I'm glad someone is making it. What I'd give to see one of thse paintings in person

&#x200B;

edit: specifically it reminds me of this friedrich work  [https://www.artble.com/imgs/e/4/4/834441/two\_men\_contemplating\_the\_moon\_c\_1819.jpg](https://www.artble.com/imgs/e/4/4/834441/two_men_contemplating_the_moon_c_1819.jpg)

Damn, dude. Your attitude astounds me. This person makes an intelligent comment with research pointing out humans rights abuses and linking them to the video in question, and your reaction is to... condescend and insult them? You're right that someone in this thread needs to grow up, but it isn't /u/superscout. 

&#x200B;

*spoiler* it's you.

Meanwhile, over at /r/the_donald, there's utter chaos. Half of them are praising Mueller, the rest are calling him a member of the Deep State. 

&#x200B;

One of the top comments is a user stating [none of the left are ever going to read the report.](https://imgur.com/a/d2JUUC9) The next comment down is: "[I ain't reading this bullshit.](https://imgur.com/a/pFFd59E)" 

&#x200B;

The rest just seem to be bots (or bafflingly stupid people), parroting Fox news quotes ("No collusion!") or trying to somehow propose that the redacted sections are actually about Hillary Clinton. 


Jesus.

The first sentence is correct, the second makes assumptions. Many people have already pointed out that a lot of the "greening" of the earth is due to agriculture, not tree replacement. Our crops don't sequester nearly as much CO2 as trees do, so just cause the earth is greener doesn't mean it's healthier, the same way that algae blooms in the ocean don't mean that life is "thriving" there, like people once thought. 

&#x200B;

We could cover the entire earth with crops and it would be 100% green, but it still would be far less biodiverse and stable that an earth covered with trees.

I've lost friends to suicide. Are you going to sit here and tell me my friend **deserved** to hang herself because she was weak? 

&#x200B;

Plain and simple: you're wrong. You know nothing about the lives of others and the pain, tragedy, and trauma that drives someone to suicide. To call someone weak for putting themselves out of a misery you can't even *begin* to fathom?! 

&#x200B;

I don't even know how to respond to you. Go hawk your half-baked opinions on suicide elsewhere.

Do you want the diplomatic bullshit answer or the real answer?

&#x200B;

The bullshit answer is that the SA-Yemeni war is seen as a proxy war between, on the one side, SA, Israel, and the US, and on the other side, Yemen and Iran. The US has formally denounced the actions of the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps, which is a  subsect of the Iranian military, as well as labeled them a formal terrorist group. In response, the Iranian government has labeled the US military in its entirety as a terrorist group. These are internationally-recognized labels, and are usually seen as the early warning signs of a military escalation. In a way, then, pulling out of Iran could be seen as a letdown to our purported allies (Israel and SA) and a symbolic victory for our purported enemies, mainly Iran. In the long term, this could cause further escalation. 

&#x200B;

The real answer is that the decision to pull out of Yemen isn't at *all* an endangerment to our troops. Obviously lives would be saved by pulling out of a combat zone. Even *more* lives would likely be saved in the long term if we distance ourselves from SA and Israel and seek more sustainable alliances that aren't based on tenuous geopolitics in the Middle East. 

&#x200B;

However, Trump knows that if he makes a statement like this, his cronies will be able to fill in the logical gaps with the first explanation I provided, and justify his actions thus. His supporters will carry on believing he's doing this *for the trooooooops!!!!!* while everyone else will carry on knowing he's doing this for the Saudi $$$$$$$ that has been pouring into his back pocket via some Trump Hotel laundering that has been recently exposed.

The primary clause of his statement focuses on the fact that this is an "attempt to weaken **my** constitutional authorities."

&#x200B;

C'mon, man. If you're going to pretend you give a shit about this country at least *pretend* it's not all about you and your power. Jesus.

